  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Job",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 35,
    "summary": "Elihu contrasts the weakness of man and the power of God—Our wickedness hurts other men, and our righteousness helps them—Man should trust in the Lord.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Elihu spake moreover, and said,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:1",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Thinkest thou this to be right, that thou saidst, My righteousness is more than God’s?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 32,
            "end": 36
          },
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:2",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "For thou saidst, What advantage will it be unto thee? and, What profit shall I have, if I be cleansed from my sin?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 58
          },
          {
            "start": 85,
            "end": 101
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:3",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "I will answer thee, and thy companions with thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:4",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Look unto the heavens, and see; and behold the clouds which are higher than thou.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:5",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou sinnest, what doest thou against him? or if thy transgressions be multiplied, what doest thou unto him?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 51
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:6",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "If thou be righteous, what givest thou him? or what receiveth he of thine hand?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "Prov. 9:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Prov. 9:12.",
            "prettyString": "Proverbs 9:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "proverbs",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 9,
                    "end": 9,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:7",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "Thy wickedness may hurt a man as thou art; and thy righteousness may profit the son of man.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 23
          },
          {
            "start": 38,
            "end": 42
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:8",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "By reason of the multitude of oppressions they make the oppressed to cry: they cry out by reason of the arm of the mighty.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:9",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "But none saith, Where is God my maker, who giveth songs in the night;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "Ps. 77:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 22,
            "end": 24
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Ps. 77:6.",
            "prettyString": "Psalms 77:6",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "psalms",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 77,
                    "end": 77,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 6,
                        "end": 6
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:10",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Who teacheth us more than the beasts of the earth, and maketh us wiser than the fowls of heaven?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:11",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "There they cry, but none giveth answer, because of the pride of evil men.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:12",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Surely God will not hear vanity, neither will the Almighty regard it.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:13",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Although thou sayest thou shalt not see him, yet judgment is before him; therefore trust thou in him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          },
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 60
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:14",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "But now, because it is not so, he hath visited in his anger; yet he knoweth it not in great extremity:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 22
          },
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:15",
        "book": "Job",
        "chapter": 35,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore doth Job open his mouth in vain; he multiplieth words without knowledge.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Job 35:16",
